      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm working on a new credit scoring model for a fintech startup. we're trying to move beyond just traditional FICO/credit history and incorporate more \"environmental\" data to better predict long-term default risk. specifically, i wanted to get your thoughts on how we should weigh factors like neighborhood volatility and community cohesion. from a quant perspective, how do these act as indicators for loan stability?",
