      "role": "user",
      "content": "makes sense. but how would we actually quantify \"community cohesion\" or \"volatility\" in the data? like, if we're looking at hyper-local data, what are the actual metrics or proxies we should be pulling to differentiate a \"stable\" neighborhood from one that's more transient or unpredictable? we want to make sure we aren't just looking at income, but the actual social fabric of the area.",
