    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense for the model's accuracy, but i'm worried about the regulatory side of things—specifically regarding fair lending laws and \"redlining\" concerns. if we start weighting things like residential turnover rates or certain types of local retail density, aren't we basically just creating proxies for racial demographics or socioeconomic status? how do we balance getting a \"real\" picture of neighborhood stability without the model accidentally penalizing specific ethnic or minority communities that happen to live in more transient or urban areas?",
